              when calling setPermissions or resetPermissions, but present
              for the results of permission queries.
          principal: User or group receiving access in the form of
              \"login\" for local or \"DOMAIN\\login\" for users in a Windows domain.
          group: Whether principal refers to a user or a group.
              
              True for
              a group and false for a user.
          roleId: Reference to the role providing the access.
          propagate: Whether or not this permission propagates down the hierarchy
