   `pyVmomi.vmodl.fault.NotSupported` fault.
   
   Support for some features is indicated by the presence or absence of
   the manager object from the service instance. For example, the AlarmManager manager
   object indicates collecting alarms is supported.
   Other features indicate whether or not a given operation on an
   object throws a `pyVmomi.vmodl.fault.NotSupported` fault.
   
   Some capabilities depend on the host or virtual machine
   version. These are specified by using the vim.host.Capability and
   vim.vm.Capability objects.
   
   Attributes:
       provisioningSupported: Indicates whether or not the service instance supports provisioning.
           
           For example, the `pyVmomi.vim.VirtualMachine.clone` operation.
       multiHostSupported: Indicates whether or not the service instance supports multiple hosts.
       userShellAccessSupported: Flag indicating whether host user accounts should have the option to
           be granted shell access
       supportedEVCMode: All supported Enhanced VMotion Compatibility modes.
       supportedEVCGraphicsMode: All supported Enhanced VMotion Compatibility Graphics modes.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.1.0
       networkBackupAndRestoreSupported: Indicates whether network backup and restore feature is supported.
       ftDrsWithoutEvcSupported: Is DRS supported for Fault Tolerance VMs without enabling EVC.
       hciWorkflowSupported: Specifies if the workflow for setting up a HCI cluster is supported.
       computePolicyVersion: Specifies the supported compute policy version.
       lifecycleManagementSupported: Specifies if lifecycle management of a Cluster is supported.
       hostSeedingSupported: Specifies if host seeding for a cluster is supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.2.0
       scalableSharesSupported: Specifies if scalable shares for resource pools is supported.
       hadcsSupported: Specifies if highly available distributed clustering service is supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.1.1
       configMgmtSupported: Specifies if desired configuration management platform is supported
           on the cluster.
           
