              Typically, a more specific subclass, such as NoDiskSpace, will be thrown.
          pyVmomi.vim.fault.OutOfBounds: if Host.capability.maxSupportedVMs is exceeded.
          pyVmomi.vim.fault.DuplicateName: if another virtual machine in the same folder already has
              the specified target name.
          pyVmomi.vim.fault.InvalidName: if the name is not a valid entity name.
          pyVmomi.vim.fault.InvalidDatastore: if the operation cannot be performed on the
              target datastores.
          pyVmomi.vim.fault.InsufficientResourcesFault: if this operation would violate a resource
