          hostMap: Map of URLs for leased hosts for a given datastore.
              
              This is used to
              look up multi-POST-capable hosts for a datastore.
      """
      lease: HttpNfcLease
      entity: ManagedEntity
      deviceUrl: list[HttpNfcLease.DeviceUrl] = []
      totalDiskCapacityInKB: pyVmomi.VmomiSupport.long
      leaseTimeout: int
      hostMap: list[HttpNfcLease.DatastoreLeaseInfo] = []

   class DeviceUrl(pyVmomi.vmodl.DynamicData):
      """
      Provides a mapping from logical device IDs to upload/download
      URLs.
      
      For export, a single device id is returned based on the object
      identifiers for the objects.
      
      For import, two device ids are returned. One based on the object
      names used in the ImportSpec, and one based on the object
      identifiers for the created objects. This is immutable and would
      match the id if an ExportLease is latter created.
      
      Attributes:
          key: The immutable identifier for the device.
              
              This is set for both import/export
              leases.
          importKey: Identifies the device based on the names in an ImportSpec.
              
              This is only
              set for import leases.
          url: The URL to use to upload/download the device content.
              
              The returned url contains either an IP address, a hostname or a \"*\". If a
              \"*\" is returned the client must substitutes the \"*\" with the hostname
              or IP address used when connecting to the server.
              For example if the client connected to \"someHost\" and the device
              url returned is:
              
                   http:// *:somePort/somePath
              the client must substitute the \"*\" with \"someHost\" before use. The resulting
              url would be:
              
                   http://someHost:somePort/somePath
              The server cannot return a valid hostname or IP address when the client
              connects via a NAT, a proxy, or when the server is multihomed.
          sslThumbprint: SSL thumbprint for the host the URL refers to.
              
              Empty if no SSL thumbprint
              is available or needed.
          sslCertificate: PEM encoded SSL Certificate of the host
              
              Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
          disk: Optional value to specify if the attached file is a disk in
              vmdk format.
          targetId: Id for this target.
              
              This only used for multi-POSTing, where a single HTTP
              POST is applied to multiple targets.
          datastoreKey: Key for the datastore this disk is on.
              
              This is used to look up hosts
              which can be used to multi-POST disk contents, in the host map of the
              lease.
          fileSize: Specifies the size of the file backing for this device.
              
              This property
              is only set for non-disk file backings.
      """
      key: str
      importKey: str
      url: str
      sslThumbprint: str
      sslCertificate: _typing.Optional[str] = None
      disk: _typing.Optional[bool] = None
      targetId: _typing.Optional[str] = None
      datastoreKey: _typing.Optional[str] = None
      fileSize: _typing.Optional[pyVmomi.VmomiSupport.long] = None

   class ManifestEntry(pyVmomi.vmodl.DynamicData):
      """
      Provides a manifest for downloaded (exported) files and disks.
      
      Attributes:
          key: Key used to match this entry with the corresponding `pyVmomi.vim.HttpNfcLease.DeviceUrl`
              entry in `pyVmomi.vim.HttpNfcLease.info`.
          sha1: SHA-1 checksum of the data stream sent from the server.
              
              This can be used
              to verify that the bytes received by the client match those sent by the
              HttpNfc server.
          checksum: Checksum of the data stream sent/recieved by host.
              
              See `pyVmomi.vim.HttpNfcLease.ManifestEntry.ChecksumType` for used algorithm.
          checksumType: Algorithm used to produce checksum in respective property.
              
              See `pyVmomi.vim.HttpNfcLease.ManifestEntry.ChecksumType` for supported algorithms.
          size: Size of the downloaded file.
          disk: True if the downloaded file is a virtual disk backing.
          capacity: The capacity of the disk, if the file is a virtual disk backing.
          populatedSize: The populated size of the disk, if the file is a virtual disk backing.
      """
      class ChecksumType(pyVmomi.VmomiSupport.Enum):
